        "id": 145675,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-28T18:41:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><span>Your interpretation is correct for both cards.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Kaargra is dealing the two instances of damage seperately, so the HP order is recalculated both times. &nbsp;If I had three heroes: AA [24], AZ [23], and OX [22], then she would hit AA for 4 (AZ [23] OX [22] AA [20]) and then hit OX for 3 (AZ [23], AA [20], OX [19]).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If the text was something along the lines of \"Kaargra hits the two highest for 4\", then it would not be recalculated and you would hit AA and AZ. &nbsp;But as it is, the two attacks are entirely seperate.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:28.942Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
