        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Your interpretation is correct for both cards.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Kaargra is dealing the two instances of damage seperately, so the HP order is recalculated both times. &nbsp;If I had three heroes: AA [24], AZ [23], and OX [22], then she would hit AA for 4 (AZ [23] OX [22] AA [20]) and then hit OX for 3 (AZ [23], AA [20], OX [19]).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If the text was something along the lines of &quot;Kaargra hits the two highest for 4&quot;, then it would not be recalculated and you would hit AA and AZ. &nbsp;But as it is, the two attacks are entirely seperate.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
