        "id": 145676,
        "name": "aawood",
        "username": "aawood",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/8e8cbc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-07-29T11:39:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm with Donner here; given the wording, it strongly implies it's meant to target the two people then do the damage; Otherwise, I'd expect it to say \"Khgraa hits the target with the highest HP for 4. Khagraa hits the target with the second highest HP for 3.\" or possibly \"Khgraa hits the target with the highest HP for 4, then hits the target with the second highest HP for 3.\"</p><p>If this is wrong, I'm having trouble thinking how I'd word such a card if it *was* meant to hit two targets no matter what... perhaps \"Khagraa hits the target with the highest HP for 4, then Khagraa hits the target other than the first target with the highest HP for 3\", but that seems wordy, and would lead to Dual Crowbar levels of \"what happens when the first target is immune? What happens if that damage is redirected? What what what?\".</p>",
