      {
        "id": 145679,
        "name": "aawood",
        "username": "aawood",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/8e8cbc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-08-03T11:33:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p><span>\"Kaargra deals the highest hp hero 4 damage. &nbsp;Kaargra deals a different hero with the second. . .\"</span></p></blockquote><p><span>I'm not sure that wording would work.&nbsp;</span></p><p>Characters A, B and C have 20, 17, 14 health. Kaargra deals the highest HP target (A) 4 damage. This leaves us with B on 17, A on 16, C on 14.</p><p>Kaargra then hits \"the different hero with the second highest health\" for 3. Who is that? A has the second highest health currently, but is not a different hero. B was the second highest health, but has the highest at the point the second attack happens. C has the *third* highest health overall, and has since the start... but has the second highest of all the \"different\" heros (and would even if the first attack hadn't changed the order of A and B).</p><p>And you're right, the app is official, I'll be glad when WotC is released and we can see how the card as-worded works for certain!</p><p>(Side note; how the heck was I spelling Kaargra in that last post?!?)</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:29.225Z",
