        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<blockquote><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51); font-family: 'Open Sans', HelveticaNeue, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14.3999996185303px; line-height: 21.5999984741211px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">&quot;Kaargra deals the highest hp hero 4 damage. &nbsp;Kaargra deals a different hero with the second. . .&quot;</span></p></blockquote><p><span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">I&#39;m not sure that wording would work.&nbsp;</span></p><p>Characters A, B and C have 20, 17, 14 health. Kaargra deals the highest HP target (A) 4 damage. This leaves us with B on 17, A on 16, C on 14.</p><p>Kaargra then hits &quot;the different hero with the second highest health&quot; for 3. Who is that? A has the second highest health currently, but is not a different hero. B was the second highest health, but has the highest at the point the second attack happens. C has the *third* highest health overall, and has since the start... but has the second highest of all the &quot;different&quot; heros (and would even if the first attack hadn&#39;t changed the order of A and B).</p><p>And you&#39;re right, the app is official, I&#39;ll be glad when WotC is released and we can see how the card as-worded works for certain!</p><p>(Side note; how the heck was I spelling Kaargra in that last post?!?)</p>",
